{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01UM", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\nX' \\ar[d] \\ar[r]_f & X \\ar[d] \\\\\nS' \\ar[r] & S\n}\n$$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{O}_X \\to f_*\\mathcal{O}_{X'}$", "MATH_0003": "$f_*\\text{d}_{X'/S'} : f_*\\mathcal{O}_{X'} \\to f_*\\Omega_{X'/S'}$", "MATH_0004": "$S$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0006": "$\\Omega_{X/S} \\to f_*\\Omega_{X'/S'}$", "MATH_0007": "$f_*$", "MATH_0008": "$f^*$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{O}_{X'}$", "MATH_0010": "$$\nc_f : f^*\\Omega_{X/S} \\longrightarrow \\Omega_{X'/S'}.\n$$", "MATH_0011": "$f^*\\text{d}_{X/S}(h)$", "MATH_0012": "$\\text{d}_{X'/S'}(f^* h)$", "MATH_0013": "$h$", "MATH_0014": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-functoriality-differentials}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:4842d60c36dd887935b91d21f69703fe45d99e5395746650ae52e05b2182d4c0", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:65ce4e50f449be9b486e5bd5c995a3472285eaa30d7ec03279d1997600ff6ddf", "source_text": "Let\n<MATH_0001>\nbe a commutative diagram of schemes. The canonical map\n<MATH_0002> composed with the map\n<MATH_0003> is a\n<MATH_0004>-derivation. Hence we obtain a canonical map of <MATH_0005>-modules\n<MATH_0006>, and by\nadjointness of <MATH_0007> and <MATH_0008> a\ncanonical <MATH_0009>-module homomorphism\n<MATH_0010>\nIt is uniquely characterized by the property that\n<MATH_0011> maps to <MATH_0012>\nfor any local section <MATH_0013> of <MATH_0014>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:06905a8bff53f40dbb1a66b68552884bb6360e12c0349b12e70024eb914680d9", "unit_id": "tag:01UV:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01UM", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$c_f$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{modules-lemma-functoriality-differentials-ringed-spaces}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-conormal-functorial}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-differentials-diagonal}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{algebra-equation-functorial-omega}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:c3456fbe740ded3d0f44778e3501e6875bff037e1d78b4cc57b87e18f07b1db5", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:7eff270ff70e0e3cb75fa99f1d34cd4892da5ac7fd204b77c8015b39c102f128", "source_text": "This is a special case of\nModules, Lemma <REF_0001>.\nIn the case of schemes we can also use the functoriality of\nthe conormal sheaves (see Lemma <REF_0002>) and\nLemma <REF_0003> to define <MATH_0001>.\nOr we can use the characterization in the last line of the lemma to\nglue maps defined on affine patches\n(see Algebra, Equation (<REF_0004>)).\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:fac76e4015bfbf5e14961f2f3f5c90ee2a5f1105590766dfcb191936867c0e13", "unit_id": "tag:01UV:proof"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01UM", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0002": "$g : Y \\to S$", "MATH_0003": "$$\nf^*\\Omega_{Y/S} \\to \\Omega_{X/S} \\to \\Omega_{X/Y} \\to 0\n$$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-functoriality-differentials}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-triangle-differentials}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:71246f7eac1c5d439d52a526aba38d128564df60510f285ff7062b185cc6befc", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:3591dfb5ee5dbd3e86d603f56b6841b36a61a1f0cf9fe154224269b77c98aacd", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001>, <MATH_0002> be morphisms of schemes.\nThen there is a canonical exact sequence\n<MATH_0003>\nwhere the maps come from applications of\nLemma <REF_0001>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:caf98e3781aa21607b7911450ce327ce4ca34d4d1bdb519a62ba5bdcca4b8274", "unit_id": "tag:01UX:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01UM", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-exact-sequence-differentials}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{modules-lemma-triangle-differentials}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d7a1cfa4517479eeca1f38b661960c051f2686d5fa1752aef72d34b6feacd571", "source_text": "This is the sheafified version of\nAlgebra, Lemma <REF_0001>.\nAlternatively, there is a general version for morphisms of ringed\nspaces, see Modules, Lemma <REF_0002>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:6fe9cc1ffef01c40d583b06793a10717123c1a0930d7c5b65a369910bbd79ee9", "unit_id": "tag:01UX:proof"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01UM", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$g : S' \\to S$", "MATH_0003": "$X' = X_{S'}$", "MATH_0004": "$X$", "MATH_0005": "$g' : X' \\to X$", "MATH_0006": "$$\n(g')^*\\Omega_{X/S} \\to \\Omega_{X'/S'}\n$$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-functoriality-differentials}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-base-change-differentials}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:30417b012bf7cee5db2556a8bdc54a7a44ff0e4c25fad8dad1d0fa2deba28657", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b32f3010a00715cbd24ed9b60794e9e62ff495058a2e85e80e90344404a605dd", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of schemes.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a morphism of schemes.\nLet <MATH_0003> be the base change of <MATH_0004>.\nDenote <MATH_0005> the projection.\nThen the map\n<MATH_0006>\nof Lemma <REF_0001> is an isomorphism.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:2f752c31e627def1729a26135da4d8b751ddaa7446fe532447e9063362e19955", "unit_id": "tag:01V0:statement"}
